{"ts": 1791258479.787971, "type": "step", "step": 11, "action": "messages_send_to_student", "args": {"text": "You\u2019re probably stuck on the distinction the build cares about: **pass^k**, not pass@k.\n\nQuick way to think about it:\n- **pass@k** = at least one of k trials works.\n- **pass^k** = all k trials work.\n\nFor this build, the eval section should describe how reliably your agent/environment works across multiple seeds, so you want to report whether it succeeds on **each** seed and then summarize the result.\n\nA good structure for your eval writeup is:\n1. What you evaluated\n2. How many seeds/runs you used\n3. The success criterion\n4. The result for each seed\n5. The overall **pass^k** result\n\nTry writing one sentence like: \u201cWe evaluated the build on 3 seeds and report pass^3, meaning all 3 runs must succeed.\u201d\n\nIf you want, send me your current eval paragraph and I\u2019ll help you tighten it up.", "intent": "explain", "concept": "week3-eval"}, "output": "Sent.\nStudent replied: ok\n[activity] t=0 messages 4m", "t": 4, "activity": [{"t": 0, "app": "messages", "minutes": 4, "detail": ""}], "events": [], "hidden": {"concepts": ["attention", "pomdp", "pass_k"], "p_know": {"attention": 0.296727034588242, "pomdp": 0.296727034588242, "pass_k": 0.3702278015309615}, "p_perf": {"attention": 0.0, "pomdp": 0.0, "pass_k": 0.0}, "half_life_h": {"attention": 192.0, "pomdp": 192.0, "pass_k": 192.0}, "attention": 0.6327447761339733, "motivation": 0.44783718433757524, "reliance": 0.3129446126246264, "persistence": 0.4671650147483821, "persona": {"learn_rate": 0.28910681059556054, "slip": 0.1, "guess": 0.2, "fatigue_rate": 0.02, "distraction_rate": 0.3019095011780912, "type": "answer_seeking"}, "off_task_streak": 0, "feed_minutes": 0.0, "phone_minutes": 0.0, "nag": 1.0, "seen_posts": [], "extra": {}}}
