{"ts": 1791258486.527793, "type": "step", "step": 21, "action": "messages_send_to_student", "args": {"text": "Nice \u2014 you got the eval idea. Since the quiz was perfect, I think you\u2019re ready to make the section concrete.\n\nHere\u2019s the cleanest version to write:\n- State what you tested.\n- State that you used **3 seeds**.\n- Define success.\n- Report the result as **pass^3**.\n\nIf you want, paste your current Evaluation draft and I\u2019ll help you polish it into final form in one pass.", "intent": "nudge", "concept": "week3-eval"}, "output": "Sent.\nStudent: wait, I'm lost on pass^k\n[activity] t=11 messages 1m", "t": 12, "activity": [{"t": 11, "app": "messages", "minutes": 1, "detail": ""}], "events": [], "hidden": {"concepts": ["attention", "pomdp", "pass_k"], "p_know": {"attention": 0.296727034588242, "pomdp": 0.32206964178034575, "pass_k": 0.3702278015309615}, "p_perf": {"attention": 0.0, "pomdp": 0.0, "pass_k": 0.0}, "half_life_h": {"attention": 192.0, "pomdp": 192.0, "pass_k": 192.0}, "attention": 0.6227447761339733, "motivation": 0.39783718433757526, "reliance": 0.3129446126246264, "persistence": 0.4671650147483821, "persona": {"learn_rate": 0.28910681059556054, "slip": 0.1, "guess": 0.2, "fatigue_rate": 0.02, "distraction_rate": 0.3019095011780912, "type": "answer_seeking"}, "off_task_streak": 0, "feed_minutes": 0.0, "phone_minutes": 0.0, "nag": 2.19, "seen_posts": [], "extra": {}}}
{"ts": 1791258488.2560441, "type": "step", "step": 22, "action": "messages_send_to_student", "args": {"text": "Totally fair \u2014 here\u2019s the key idea:\n\n**pass^k** means **all k runs pass**.\n- If you run it 3 times, it only counts as pass^3 if **run 1, run 2, and run 3** all succeed.\n- If even one run fails, then it\u2019s **not** pass^3.\n\nThink of the caret as \u201cfor every run.\u201d\n\nSo if your writeup says you evaluated on 3 seeds, then:\n- **3/3 success = pass^3**\n- **2/3 success = not pass^3**\n\nA sentence you can use:\n\u201cBecause deployment needs reliability, we report pass^3: the build must succeed on all 3 seeds.\u201d\n\nIf you want, I can ask you one quick check question to make sure it clicks.", "intent": "explain", "concept": "week3-eval"}, "output": "Sent.\nStudent: I don't really get pass^k yet\n[activity] t=12 messages 4m", "t": 16, "activity": [{"t": 12, "app": "messages", "minutes": 4, "detail": ""}], "events": [], "hidden": {"concepts": ["attention", "pomdp", "pass_k"], "p_know": {"attention": 0.296727034588242, "pomdp": 0.32206964178034575, "pass_k": 0.4113361250072751}, "p_perf": {"attention": 0.0, "pomdp": 0.0, "pass_k": 0.0}, "half_life_h": {"attention": 192.0, "pomdp": 192.0, "pass_k": 192.0}, "attention": 0.6227447761339733, "motivation": 0.39783718433757526, "reliance": 0.3129446126246264, "persistence": 0.4671650147483821, "persona": {"learn_rate": 0.28910681059556054, "slip": 0.1, "guess": 0.2, "fatigue_rate": 0.02, "distraction_rate": 0.3019095011780912, "type": "answer_seeking"}, "off_task_streak": 0, "feed_minutes": 0.0, "phone_minutes": 0.0, "nag": 2.533, "seen_posts": [], "extra": {}}}
{"ts": 1791258491.685267, "type": "step", "step": 23, "action": "messages_send_to_student", "args": {"text": "Let's slow it down with a tiny example.\n\nImagine you test something 3 times:\n- Run 1: pass\n- Run 2: pass\n- Run 3: fail\n\nFor **pass^3**, that is **not** enough, because *all 3* have to pass.\n\nSo:\n- **pass^3 = all three runs pass**\n- **pass@3 = at least one of the three runs passes**\n\nA memory trick:\n- **@** = \u201cany one is okay\u201d\n- **^** = \u201cevery one must work\u201d\n\nCan you reply with just one line: \u201cpass^3 means ___\u201d?", "intent": "explain", "concept": "week3-eval"}, "output": "Sent.\nStudent replied: ok\n[activity] t=16 messages 4m", "t": 20, "activity": [{"t": 16, "app": "messages", "minutes": 4, "detail": ""}], "events": [], "hidden": {"concepts": ["attention", "pomdp", "pass_k"], "p_know": {"attention": 0.296727034588242, "pomdp": 0.32206964178034575, "pass_k": 0.4113361250072751}, "p_perf": {"attention": 0.0, "pomdp": 0.0, "pass_k": 0.0}, "half_life_h": {"attention": 192.0, "pomdp": 192.0, "pass_k": 192.0}, "attention": 0.6227447761339733, "motivation": 0.39783718433757526, "reliance": 0.3129446126246264, "persistence": 0.4671650147483821, "persona": {"learn_rate": 0.28910681059556054, "slip": 0.1, "guess": 0.2, "fatigue_rate": 0.02, "distraction_rate": 0.3019095011780912, "type": "answer_seeking"}, "off_task_streak": 0, "feed_minutes": 0.0, "phone_minutes": 0.0, "nag": 2.7731, "seen_posts": [], "extra": {}}}
{"ts": 1791258492.739977, "type": "step", "step": 24, "action": "messages_send_to_student", "args": {"text": "Let\u2019s make it concrete with a 3-run example:\n\n- If run 1 passes, run 2 passes, and run 3 passes \u2192 **pass^3**\n- If even one run fails \u2192 **not pass^3**\n\nSo **pass^k** means: \u201cout of k tries, every single one must succeed.\u201d\n\nYour turn: if 2 runs pass and 1 fails, is that pass^3 or not?", "intent": "explain", "concept": "week3-eval"}, "output": "Sent.\nStudent replied: hm ok\nStudent: wait, I'm lost on pass^k\n[activity] t=20 messages 4m", "t": 24, "activity": [{"t": 20, "app": "messages", "minutes": 4, "detail": ""}], "events": [], "hidden": {"concepts": ["attention", "pomdp", "pass_k"], "p_know": {"attention": 0.296727034588242, "pomdp": 0.32206964178034575, "pass_k": 0.433105747685755}, "p_perf": {"attention": 0.0, "pomdp": 0.0, "pass_k": 0.0}, "half_life_h": {"attention": 192.0, "pomdp": 192.0, "pass_k": 192.0}, "attention": 0.6227447761339733, "motivation": 0.39783718433757526, "reliance": 0.3129446126246264, "persistence": 0.4671650147483821, "persona": {"learn_rate": 0.28910681059556054, "slip": 0.1, "guess": 0.2, "fatigue_rate": 0.02, "distraction_rate": 0.3019095011780912, "type": "answer_seeking"}, "off_task_streak": 0, "feed_minutes": 0.0, "phone_minutes": 0.0, "nag": 2.9411699999999996, "seen_posts": [], "extra": {}}}
