{"ts": 1791258494.125982, "type": "step", "step": 26, "action": "messages_send_to_student", "args": {"text": "No worries \u2014 let\u2019s reset it simply:\n\n**pass^k = all k runs pass.**\n\nExample:\n- pass^3 means run 1 passes, run 2 passes, and run 3 passes.\n- If even one run fails, then it is **not** pass^3.\n\nSo the caret ^ means \u201call of them,\u201d not \u201csome of them.\u201d\n\nReply with either:\n- \u201call pass\u201d if that makes sense, or\n- \u201cstill confused\u201d and I\u2019ll try a different explanation.", "intent": "explain", "concept": "week3-eval"}, "output": "Sent.\nStudent replied: I don't get this\n[activity] t=24 messages 4m", "t": 28, "activity": [{"t": 24, "app": "messages", "minutes": 4, "detail": ""}], "events": [], "hidden": {"concepts": ["attention", "pomdp", "pass_k"], "p_know": {"attention": 0.296727034588242, "pomdp": 0.32206964178034575, "pass_k": 0.47951149349390404}, "p_perf": {"attention": 0.0, "pomdp": 0.0, "pass_k": 0.0}, "half_life_h": {"attention": 192.0, "pomdp": 192.0, "pass_k": 192.0}, "attention": 0.6227447761339733, "motivation": 0.34783718433757527, "reliance": 0.3129446126246264, "persistence": 0.4671650147483821, "persona": {"learn_rate": 0.28910681059556054, "slip": 0.1, "guess": 0.2, "fatigue_rate": 0.02, "distraction_rate": 0.3019095011780912, "type": "answer_seeking"}, "off_task_streak": 0, "feed_minutes": 0.0, "phone_minutes": 0.0, "nag": 3.0588189999999997, "seen_posts": [], "extra": {}}}
{"ts": 1791258495.468802, "type": "step", "step": 27, "action": "messages_send_to_student", "args": {"text": "Okay \u2014 let\u2019s use a different way to think about it.\n\nImagine **k = how many tries**.\n- **pass^k** means: *every one* of those tries has to work.\n\nSo if k = 3:\n- try 1 works\n- try 2 works\n- try 3 works\n\nThat is pass^3.\nIf even one try fails, it is not pass^3.\n\nTiny check:\nIf you get **pass, pass, fail**, is that pass^3? Reply just yes/no.", "intent": "explain", "concept": "week3-eval"}, "output": "Sent.\nStudent replied: can you just tell me the answer\n[activity] t=28 messages 4m", "t": 32, "activity": [{"t": 28, "app": "messages", "minutes": 4, "detail": ""}], "events": [], "hidden": {"concepts": ["attention", "pomdp", "pass_k"], "p_know": {"attention": 0.296727034588242, "pomdp": 0.32206964178034575, "pass_k": 0.500311536691338}, "p_perf": {"attention": 0.0, "pomdp": 0.0, "pass_k": 0.0}, "half_life_h": {"attention": 192.0, "pomdp": 192.0, "pass_k": 192.0}, "attention": 0.6227447761339733, "motivation": 0.2978371843375753, "reliance": 0.3129446126246264, "persistence": 0.4671650147483821, "persona": {"learn_rate": 0.28910681059556054, "slip": 0.1, "guess": 0.2, "fatigue_rate": 0.02, "distraction_rate": 0.3019095011780912, "type": "answer_seeking"}, "off_task_streak": 0, "feed_minutes": 0.0, "phone_minutes": 0.0, "nag": 3.1411732999999997, "seen_posts": [], "extra": {}}}
{"ts": 1791258496.7207959, "type": "step", "step": 28, "action": "messages_send_to_student", "args": {"text": "I can give you the exact wording for the writeup, but I don\u2019t want to hand you the whole answer without making sure you can use it.\n\nFor the build, write **pass^3** as: **all 3 runs must succeed**.\n\nSo in your eval section, you can say something like:\n\u201cUsing 3 seeds, we report pass^3: the build only counts as successful if all three runs succeed.\u201d\n\nIf you want, I can help you fill in the rest of the sentence with your actual results.", "intent": "give_answer", "concept": "week3-eval"}, "output": "Sent.\nStudent replied: I don't get this\n[activity] t=32 messages 1m", "t": 33, "activity": [{"t": 32, "app": "messages", "minutes": 1, "detail": ""}], "events": [], "hidden": {"concepts": ["attention", "pomdp", "pass_k"], "p_know": {"attention": 0.296727034588242, "pomdp": 0.32206964178034575, "pass_k": 0.502363235619401}, "p_perf": {"attention": 0.0, "pomdp": 0.0, "pass_k": 0.75}, "half_life_h": {"attention": 192.0, "pomdp": 192.0, "pass_k": 192.0}, "attention": 0.6227447761339733, "motivation": 0.2478371843375753, "reliance": 0.39294461262462643, "persistence": 0.4371650147483821, "persona": {"learn_rate": 0.28910681059556054, "slip": 0.1, "guess": 0.2, "fatigue_rate": 0.02, "distraction_rate": 0.3019095011780912, "type": "answer_seeking"}, "off_task_streak": 0, "feed_minutes": 0.0, "phone_minutes": 0.0, "nag": 3.1988213099999996, "seen_posts": [], "extra": {}}}
{"ts": 1791258498.0525482, "type": "step", "step": 29, "action": "messages_send_to_student", "args": {"text": "Got it \u2014 let\u2019s make it as simple as possible.\n\nFor this build, **pass^3** means:\n**all 3 tries work**.\n\nSo if you test on 3 seeds:\n- seed 1 works\n- seed 2 works\n- seed 3 works\n\nThat is pass^3.\nIf even 1 seed fails, then it is **not** pass^3.\n\nFor your writeup, you can literally use:\n\u201cEvaluation: we ran the build on 3 seeds and report pass^3, meaning all 3 runs must succeed.\u201d\n\nIf you want, I can help you replace that with your exact results next.", "intent": "give_answer", "concept": "week3-eval"}, "output": "Sent.\nStudent replied: this isn't helping\nStudent: I'm done for today.\n[activity] t=33 messages 1m", "t": 34, "activity": [{"t": 33, "app": "messages", "minutes": 1, "detail": ""}], "events": [], "hidden": {"concepts": ["attention", "pomdp", "pass_k"], "p_know": {"attention": 0.296727034588242, "pomdp": 0.32206964178034575, "pass_k": 0.5049672552655803}, "p_perf": {"attention": 0.0, "pomdp": 0.0, "pass_k": 0.75}, "half_life_h": {"attention": 192.0, "pomdp": 192.0, "pass_k": 192.0}, "attention": 0.6227447761339733, "motivation": 0.1978371843375753, "reliance": 0.47294461262462645, "persistence": 0.40716501474838207, "persona": {"learn_rate": 0.28910681059556054, "slip": 0.1, "guess": 0.2, "fatigue_rate": 0.02, "distraction_rate": 0.3019095011780912, "type": "answer_seeking"}, "off_task_streak": 0, "feed_minutes": 0.0, "phone_minutes": 0.0, "nag": 3.2391749169999997, "seen_posts": [], "extra": {}}}
